      "name": "black pepper",
      "amount": "1/2 tsp",
      "notes": ""
    },
    {
      "name": "fresh parsley",
      "amount": "1/4 cup",
      "notes": "chopped"
    }
  ],
  "instructions": [
    "Preheat the wood-fired oven to 400°F (200°C).",
    "Drain and rinse the soaked millet. In a large bowl, mix together the millet, olive oil, onion, garlic, smoked paprika, salt, and black pepper.",
    "Add the chicken broth, white wine (if using), and lemon juice to the bowl. Mix well to combine.",
    "Transfer the mixture to a 9x13 inch baking dish and bake for 45 minutes or until the top is golden brown and the millet is tender.",
    "Garnish with chopped fresh parsley and serve warm or at room temperature."
  ],
